# VPS networking

By default, your VPS will be setup using `cloud-init` with the correct networking configuration. If you need to make changes to your networking configuration, you can do so by editing the appropriate configuration files for your distribution.

## Notes

To manage port forwarding, use Fyra Stack dashboard. You can run your own firewall behind Dashboard, but you must allow services through both. See the [VPS hardening guide](https://fyrastack.com/docs/vps/hardening) for more information on setting up a secondary firewall.

By default, we block SMTP traffic to your VPS (port 25). You cannot add this port to your firewall rules. If you would like to allow SMTP traffic, contact us at [support@fyralabs.com](mailto:support@fyralabs.com?subject=Allow%20SMTP%20traffic). 
Generally, we prefer to have some history of a user's behavior before allowing SMTP traffic as it's known to cause abuse complaints. For that reason, we may deny a request for SMTP traffic unblocking if we don't have enough history of a user.

Note that spoofing MAC addresses is considered network/system abuse under our [acceptable use policy](https://fyrastack.com/terms-of-service). Our system also won't allow you to access the internet if you try to spoof your MAC address. All traffic to and from your assigned public IP must come from your assigned MAC address.

## How Our VPS Network Works

When you set up your VPS, we use [cloud-init](https://cloud-init.io/) to configure your networking. This includes assigning your static IP address, MAC address, routes, DNS, interface name, and disabling DHCP. If you're curious for an example cloud-init configuration, here's one (with information redacted):

```yaml
version: 2
ethernets:
  public0:
    match:
      macaddress: $MAC_ADDRESS
    set-name: eth0
    dhcp4: false
    dhcp6: false
    addresses:
      - $PUBLIC_IP_V4/32
      - $PUBLIC_IP_V6/128
      - $PUBLIC_IPV6_DELEGATION/64
    routes:
      - to: $PUBLIC_GATEWAY_V4/32
        scope: link
      - to: 0.0.0.0/0
        via: $PUBLIC_GATEWAY_V4
        on-link: true
      - to: ::/0
        via: $PUBLIC_GATEWAY_V6
        on-link: true
    nameservers:
      addresses:
        - 1.1.1.1
        - 1.0.0.1
        - 2606:4700:4700::1111
        - 2606:4700:4700::1001
```

If you ever attempt to change your networking configuration and need to know how to set it back up, contact us via email at [support@fyralabs.com](mailto:support@fyralabs.com), mentioning Stack in the subject line.

On the back end, we use VyOS as our router and Proxmox for VPS firewall rules. In the near future, we plan to move to our own hypervisor solution, [Odorobo](https://github.com/FyraStack/odorobo). At that point, our firewall setup will change.
